Z||000014||Gumball||05-18-2001||01:06 AM||||Hey danny boy, I onced had the same experience with a ricer in his civic hatchback.  Its riceboy capital here in San Diego.   <BR>     I was at a stop light headed to school, and the punk, pulled over next to me and revved.  I just laughed out loud, and took a long stare at his fine primered car, I lauged even louder when i saw that the car was running on all 4 spares, you know, those small black wheels.it (clearly says "for temporary use only") hheheheh! <BR>   So the light turned green, and he screech out.  I just dove normally.  Just a block up front, a big rig cuts him, he swerved and wraped around a tree.  As he got out. i drove by slowly, honking at him, and lauging even more.  That was the best time i ever had!||||reg||1
Z||000015||thomas_l||05-18-2001||10:19 AM||||I've met one guy with a Neon RT that is pretty cool. He shows up for SCCA Solo II and is minimally riced. In fact he consistently beats alot of the Civics equipped with coffee can exhaust and a-pillar guage pods that look like a mud dauber nest. Since I like my cars to be sleepers I have fun with the street kids once in a while. I like being in 2nd gear in my 87 GT (4sp) while they are busy rowing up into 4th. Without any wings, scoops, or stickers my old GT really frustrates em!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000016||Spektyr||05-18-2001||06:04 PM||||That is true, nothing frustrates a ricer-boy more than getting beat by someone with fewer stickers, body mods, or smaller exhaust tips.<P>At least if you had a bigger exhaust tip or something he could (in his mind) explain why you're faster.<P>When I'm done with my Fiero (done being pretty much impossible, I know) it'll still look like a Fiero, but more like a 1990-something Fiero, if they'd actually been made.  People that know cars will know it's not a stock body, but it will not scream "Hey!  I'm a race car!".<P>I like my driving fun <I>without</I> tickets, thank you.  Strangely I've never been pulled over in my Town Car, and it's ALWAYS rolling over the speedlimit.<P>Sleeper is fun.  Not only does the chowder-head beside you at the light not expect you, but the cops don't spill their coffee trying to snatch up the radar gun when they see you either.||||reg||1
