Z||000038||Jay||05-20-2001||04:54 PM||||I've found all the import guys around me to be real cool.  When they see my car (86 GT with Norhtstar) they all congregate around it.  At the track I get nothin' but love from them and yes I've been beaten by Acuras and Hondas at the track.  I think it is stupid for us to make fun of import guys.  Let's face it, the Fiero is dying as a platform to modify.  Honda Civics are cheap and parts are plentiful.  You don't have to put a Northstar in a Civic to get it to go fast.  Bolt on parts is the future and unfortunately the Fiero is being left behind.  Don't get me wrong, I love the Fiero but some of the comments on this thread were boarderline racist.  I know that is a harsh word, but I think we should acknowledge that these "ricers" are doing the same types of modifications to their cars as we are...trying to get them to go faster and look unique.  We may not have the same eye for style, but any kind of modification adds personal flavour to a car.  In fact my next car will be an import...from Italy...a Ferrari, and no not a Fiero to look like a Ferrari but a genuine Marenello classic!<P><P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande||||reg||1
Z||000039||KevinP||05-20-2001||05:07 PM||||"I think we should acknowledge that these "ricers" are doing the same types of modifications to their cars as we are...trying to get them to go faster and look unique. We may not have the same eye for style, but any kind of modification adds personal flavour to a car."<P>(applause)||||reg||10
