Z||000042||danny boy||05-20-2001||08:09 PM|||| I think this needs to be said-and understood.<BR> Not everyone with an import is a ricer. the term ricer means one with a cocky attitude,no mechanical knowledge,that thinks they are better than anyone else. They have stock cars with big wings,vinyl graphics and stickers for parts they do not have. They would not know what a performance car was if they were run down by one. <BR>I have an import, too. And yes, its very fast. I have no stickers,no body kit,not even aftermarket wheels. I do have bigger turbos, big exaust with all emissions in place, and a few other things. The only badging I have is the RallyArt badges on the fenders, and the dOdGe sTealth badges are gone,too. I do have dual 3.5" tips on a 3" exaust,but thats because I could not find 3" tips to fit on the 2.5" outlets from the Flowmaster T/A muffler.<BR> Remember, just because its an Import doesn't mean its Fast,nor does it make the owner a ricer.||||reg||1
Z||000043||cadaver||05-20-2001||10:52 PM||||Well said Danny boy. Thank you.||||reg||1
Z||000044||fyerstarter||05-20-2001||11:56 PM||||I took my new Gt down to Malibu today and happened across this beautifull specimen in the Jack in the Crack parking lot.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fyerstarter.f2s.com/ricer_stang.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fyerstarter.f2s.com/ricer_stang.jpg</A> <P>The picture does not due justice to this abomination but all the yellow you see there is the "Krylon touch", there is duct tape on the bumper then Kryloned over that, every sticker known to man, and the exhausts were that bendy exhaust pipe you can buy from Pep Boys painted black sticking out about 6 inches from the bumper. <P>This is not an import and the owner was not a backwards hat boy, but it is most certainly rice. <P>My point is, Bad taste is bad taste. Don't generalize and look down on imports because some of them are ricey, just like you don't want people to think your Fiero is a fire starting piece of crap, just because some were.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000045||Pontiaddict||05-21-2001||12:05 AM||||Danny Boy, wasn't your import made in Illinois?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000046||maryjane||05-21-2001||02:57 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by spideyfoot:<BR><B>Hey you guys are really hurting my feelings<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero12_copy.jpg">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>O NO! Is that an SUV in the background? Hope sjp777 doesn't see it. see I Hate Suv's. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000047||Greg Piet||05-21-2001||10:55 AM||||Well call me ricey thats fine...<BR>The more I do to my car the ricier I get I suppose...   <B>YO!</B>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I have stickers all over my car (PFF ones too!).  I dont know why I put them on, except to say I had alot of them, and it seemed appropriate to put them on my old faded paint job.  I keep joking with my other autox buddy that I need a string of tailpipes across the back of the car and a set of 10 series tires on 18" rims, and a 5 tier wing.<P>My buddy keeps reminding me that although I drive my Fiero on the street, I actually race it too so the stickers arent that bad.  Yes I mainly autocross, but a few road races as well, and before the Eibach's a little dry lake bed rallycrossing.<P>I think I have developed a fairly tuned eye to determine whether or not the stickers are rice or race car, but it is sometimes difficult to tell.  <P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72 Race Director<BR>#47 SM<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.physics.unlv.edu/~gregpiet/Jan1617s.jpg">    <BR>Our lady of blessed acceleration dont fail me now!||||reg||1
Z||000048||88formula||05-21-2001||05:13 PM||||YO WHAT YOU TALKIN ABOUT YO. I'LL BUST A CAP IN YOUR A$$. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000049||danny boy||05-21-2001||05:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pontiaddict:<BR><B>Danny Boy, wasn't your import made in Illinois?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR> As far as I know,it was. I have looked everywhere for some kind of tag, but can't find one. I think the 3000GT/stealths were built alongside the DSM trio as they were based on them, but I won't swear to it.<BR> To be truthful, the only imports I have seen That acually were built overseas were a few VWs.On my friends old 16V Scirrocco and on his new Golf there is a tag in the doorjamb stating that the car was built in Germany.Another friend with a Golf's tag says built in Mexico. <BR> I still think everything on this planet is made in China,regardless of where it is put together.<BR>   ||||reg||1
Z||000050||cadaver||05-21-2001||08:09 PM||||I see hes got the back of the hood all jacked up in the air. Must be to let all the heat out of that fire breathing monster under the hood. <BR>What are those 4 bolt rims. Is this thing even a 5.0<BR>I just love it when they stick more than ne sticker on for the same kind of thing. Like the accel AND msd stickers.||||reg||1
Z||000051||Sleeper||05-21-2001||08:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by danny boy:<BR><B> I think this needs to be said-and understood.<BR> Not everyone with an import is a ricer. the term ricer means one with a cocky attitude,no mechanical knowledge,that thinks they are better than anyone else. They have stock cars with big wings,vinyl graphics and stickers for parts they do not have. They would not know what a performance car was if they were run down by one. <BR>I have an import, too. And yes, its very fast. I have no stickers,no body kit,not even aftermarket wheels. I do have bigger turbos, big exaust with all emissions in place, and a few other things. The only badging I have is the RallyArt badges on the fenders, and the dOdGe sTealth badges are gone,too. I do have dual 3.5" tips on a 3" exaust,but thats because I could not find 3" tips to fit on the 2.5" outlets from the Flowmaster T/A muffler.<BR> Remember, just because its an Import doesn't mean its Fast,nor does it make the owner a ricer.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>dude i know the differance between the two. but Cadaver was saying the cars in Import Tuner were p.o.s and crap, i'll say it again i've had friends who's cars were in the mag and i know all the car in the mag are done up with stickers glore but it's because they are "paying sponsors" cuz the cars are drag or top notch show cars.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000052||Black88GT||05-21-2001||08:59 PM||||I'm with sleeper on this one.  The cars in mags like Import Tuner and Sport Compact Car are nice imports.  No offense, but most of the older guys in this world can't understand.  Imports are what most of the kids like, get used to it.  You can bash it all you want but they are putting up impressive time slips and can actually take a turn unlike the muscle cars of your era's.<BR>I give credit where credit is due.  My friend swapped in a vtec motor to his CRX, put a nice body kit on it and rims.  It looks nice and is faster then probably 90% of the Fiero's on the road.  If I posted a pic here though I would get the "Thats rice" comments or whatever.  Its no different then a Fiero swapping in a 3800/V8 and adding side scoops/hood scoops/qtr. window scoops and raised wing stantions.      <BR>  <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000053||cadaver||05-21-2001||11:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>I'm with sleeper on this one.  The cars in mags like Import Tuner and Sport Compact Car are nice imports.  No offense, but most of the older guys in this world can't understand.  Imports are what most of the kids like, get used to it.  You can bash it all you want but they are putting up impressive time slips and can actually take a turn unlike the muscle cars of your era's.<BR>I give credit where credit is due.  My friend swapped in a vtec motor to his CRX, put a nice body kit on it and rims.  It looks nice and is faster then probably 90% of the Fiero's on the road.  If I posted a pic here though I would get the "Thats rice" comments or whatever.  Its no different then a Fiero swapping in a 3800/V8 and adding side scoops/hood scoops/qtr. window scoops and raised wing stantions.      <BR>  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Building a motor or swapping in something is not ricey. Adding a set or bitchen rims and tires is not ricey. Putting on a front scooped air dam or a body kit is not ricey.<BR>Its all those little vinyl stickers and the foldger's cans and the marine interiors etc.<BR>Are you with sleeper on everything else?<P>"i'd rather go with that scene cuz they dont dis fieros than go chill with the v8 boys who laugh at fieros. so take your cool guy mentality and go chill with your friends in west LA and do what fags do." (sleeper)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000054||Sleeper||05-22-2001||02:35 AM||||i wouldn't mind puttin i "foldger's can" on the fiero, hell yea they flow the same as flowmaster and dynomax etc, etc and its not like its gonna sound like a ricer cuz they straight pipe it and plus they have smaller motors it'll probably sound just like a flowy on a fiero. i've seen flowys on imports and it sounds just like all of their other exhausts.<P>dude you need to chill and stop your boo hoo hoo-ing. where does all this hatred toward imports come from?  and if you're from L.A. and you have been to West Coast Fiero, you probably seen that guy Tes, he has stickers on his fiero. does that make him a ricer?<P>and are you gonna call that stang in Fyerstarter post a ricer? no probably not cuz its a v8 and your down for them, right. <P><p>[This message has been edited by Sleeper (edited 05-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000055||cadaver||05-22-2001||10:40 PM||||You really dont have any idea do you.<BR>Yes I live in LA so why do you assume I have been to Chris's shop. I have never been there or met the man. And dont know a Tes or his car.<BR>Sound like your the one doing the boo-hooing.<P>No I wouldnt call the mustang in the other post rice. I would call it crap. Even if it did have an 8 (which I doubt) That doesnt mean anything other than it has an 8. <BR>Why are you obsessed over the fact that some things have 8's? I dont understand that.<P>Flowy? Is that your cute little way or saying flowmaster? Yes I have flowmasters on my 351 mustang. Because I can tell thge difference in the torque curve. And they dont sound too bad either.<P>See there you go again thinking that a folgers can has anything to do with the exhaust flow.<BR>i wouldn't mind puttin " "foldger's can" on the fiero, hell yea they flow the same as flowmaster and dynomax etc,"<P>Sound and flow are entirely two different things.<BR>And if you are so against it why are you calling the "rice" or "ricer"?||||reg||1
